Normal.Description:
Normal attacks generally refer to attacks that do not consume the stamina bar;
Includes attacks executed with the attack button, as well as attacks that only consume stamina;
For non-player units, any attack that does not trigger a pause in action is considered a normal attack.

The Normal and Special tags are mutually exclusive.

Special.Description:
Special attacks generally refer to attacks that consume the stamina bar;
Includes attacks executed with the skill button, or attacks that consume stamina;
For non-player units, any attack that triggers a pause in action is considered a special attack.

Unless specified otherwise, all attacks from summoned units derived from skills are considered special attacks.

The Normal and Special tags are mutually exclusive.

Direct.Description:
Direct attacks are typically caused by entities or weapon attacks;
Direct attacks can cause hit-stun and can be avoided through evasion effects.

All attacks that are not indirect are direct attacks.

Indirect.Description:
Indirect attacks are typically caused by environmental or debuff effects;
Indirect attacks do not cause hit-stun but cannot be avoided through evasion.

All attacks that are not direct are indirect attacks.

Threat.Description:
Ailments are special effects caused by dealing damage, divided into {$Keyword.PhysicalThreat.Meta} and {$Keyword.ElementalThreat.Meta};
All ailments are neither buffs nor debuffs.

For boss-type enemies, the damage and variable effects caused by ailments are halved.

ElementalThreat.Description:
Elemental ailments are divided into {$Keyword.ElementalThreatEffect.Meta} and {$Keyword.ElementalThreatStatus.Meta}.

Dealing direct elemental damage accumulates corresponding elemental ailment values, thereby triggering the corresponding elemental ailment effect;
The calculation of each elemental ailment value is independent.

ElementalThreatLevel.Description:
When receiving {$Keyword.Direct.Meta}{$Keyword.Elemental.Meta} damage, there is a chance to trigger accumulation of the corresponding elemental ailment value.

All elemental ailment accumulations have independent built-in interval timers. When elemental ailment accumulation is triggered, the timer for that element resets to 0 seconds;
The initial trigger chance for all elemental ailment accumulations is 0%. For every 0.05 seconds on the interval timer, the trigger chance increases by 5%.

When triggering elemental ailment accumulation via direct elemental damage, a random value between 2 and 4 of the corresponding elemental ailment value is accumulated. If {$Keyword.Critical.Meta} is triggered, an additional 1 point is accumulated;
If, when this accumulation is triggered, the direct elemental damage received does not exceed 1% of the target's maximum HP, the accumulated elemental ailment value is halved;
The initial maximum for all elemental ailment values is 100 points, and the minimum is always 0.

ElementalThreatEffect.Description:
As soon as elemental ailment value is accumulated, the corresponding elemental ailment effect takes effect immediately;
Some elemental ailment effects are overridden by their corresponding elemental ailment state.

The degree of elemental ailment effect varies according to the magnitude of the corresponding elemental ailment value.

SuperCancel.Description:
Linking a skill after a {$Keyword.ExtinctionArt.Meta} triggers a Super Cancel.

To trigger a Super Cancel, an additional 1 unit of Refined Qi is consumed;
Skills derived from a Super Cancel deal 15% increased damage.

DreamCancel.Description:
Linking a skill after another skill triggers a Dream Cancel.

To trigger a Dream Cancel, an additional 1 unit of Refined Qi is consumed;
Skills derived from a Dream Cancel deal 35% increased damage.
